### 🔬 AI-Powered Lung Cancer Detection Using Deep Learning & Medical Image Analytics

*Detecting lung abnormalities through Convolutional Neural Networks, Explainable AI, and Advanced Medical Imaging Techniques.*

</div>

---

## 📖 Overview

Lung cancer remains one of the leading causes of cancer-related deaths worldwide. Early diagnosis significantly improves treatment outcomes and survival rates.

The **Valerix Lung Cancer Detection System** is an advanced Deep Learning solution designed to analyze CT scan images and classify them into:

- 🟢 Normal
- 🟡 Benign
- 🔴 Malignant

The system leverages a custom-built CNN architecture (**ValerixNet**) combined with visualization and explainability techniques to provide reliable predictions and meaningful insights into model behavior.

---

## 🎯 Project Objectives

✔ Automate lung cancer detection from CT scan images

✔ Classify scans into multiple diagnostic categories

✔ Improve diagnostic efficiency using AI

✔ Provide explainable predictions through activation heatmaps

✔ Visualize model performance with comprehensive analytics

✔ Demonstrate practical healthcare AI applications

---

# 🏗️ System Architecture

```text
CT Scan Images
       │
       ▼
Data Preprocessing
       │
       ▼
Image Augmentation
       │
       ▼
ValerixNet CNN Model
       │
       ▼
Feature Extraction
       │
       ▼
Classification Layer
       │
       ▼
Prediction
 ┌─────────────┬─────────────┬─────────────┐
 │   Normal    │   Benign    │ Malignant   │
 └─────────────┴─────────────┴─────────────┘
       │
       ▼
Explainable AI Visualizations
```

---

# 🧠 Deep Learning Model

The project uses a custom Convolutional Neural Network called:

## ValerixNet

The architecture consists of:

### Feature Extraction Layers

- Multiple Convolutional Layers
- Batch Normalization
- ReLU Activation
- Max Pooling Layers
- Dropout Regularization

### Classification Layers

- Global Average Pooling
- Dense Layers
- Softmax Output Layer

### Performance Enhancements

- Early Stopping
- Learning Rate Scheduling
- Data Augmentation
- Dropout Regularization
- Batch Normalization

---

# 🔍 Classification Categories

| Class | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| 🟢 Normal | Healthy lung tissue with no abnormalities |
| 🟡 Benign | Non-cancerous lung nodules |
| 🔴 Malignant | Cancerous tissue requiring medical attention |

